{
  "scenario": "A LegalRuleML document modelling four sections of a fictional Residential Tenancies (Example) Act 2024 of Victoria. A strict rule obliges the tenant to pay rent on time, repaired by a late fee penalty; a defeasible rule obliges the landlord to give 28 days' notice to vacate, with two alternative readings, and is overridden by a defeasible rule permitting 14 days' notice where the premises are unfit; a further rule prohibits the landlord from entering without notice. Associations tie each statement to its section, the enacting authority, the jurisdiction and its in-force date, and the agents, figures and roles of the tenancy and of the drafting are recorded beside them.",
